    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0287" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d115-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-07T16:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1931—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>261. For Ambassador Dawes and Mr. Livesey. We now believe that we have the texts
                    of all documents with the exception of certain minor detail provisions and
                    Appendix 2 to the Report.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d115-f2"/> The Department has no
                    suggestions to make regarding them. It understands that it is not necessary that
                    any American representative sign or approve them. Ii any Government later
                    consults us we will say that the Protocol is not inconsistent with the
                    President’s proposal. You may so state informally.</p>
                <p>Wire any important changes of text and the text of Appendix 2 as soon as
                    available.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="55" type="source" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>This document bears the following notation by the Economic Adviser of the
                    Department of State: “Approved by Acting-Secretary [of the Treasury] Mills,
                    August 7/31. H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erbert</hi>] F[<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">eis</hi>].”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d115-f2" n="56" xml:id="d115-f2-content">
                <p>The report of the Committee of Experts, a protocol concerning Germany, and
                    certain other documents were signed in London, August 11 and 13, 1931. For
                    texts, see Great Britain, Cmd. 3947, Misc. No. 19 (1931): <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report of the International Committee of Experts
                        Respecting Suspension of Certain Inter-Governmental Debts</hi>. The United
                    States is not a signatory to any of these documents.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
